# <type>[optional scope]: <description>
#
# Type: feat, fix, docs, style, refactor, perf, test, build, ci, chore, revert
# Scope: area/module affected (optional, wrap in parens if present)
#
# Description: one-line summary in present tense, imperative mood, max 72 chars
#
# --- Optional: Commit body (multi-paragraph explanation) ---
# [Explain why the change is being made, not just what changed.
#  Line-wrap at 72 chars. One blank line between paragraphs.]
#
# --- Optional: Footers (issues, breaking changes) ---
# Closes #123
# Refs #456
# BREAKING CHANGE: [description of backward-incompatible changes]
#
# --- Examples ---
# feat(players): add Sleeper Players API knowledge bundle
# docs(sleeper/players): restructure into OKF format with 5 concepts
# chore: configure git commit template
#
# Remember:
# - One logical change per commit
# - Present tense: "add", not "added"
# - Imperative: "fix bug", not "fixes bug"
# - Reference issues when applicable
